From: Deskkin contributors
Subject: [PATCH] spi: esp32: sleep while polling a transfer

Let other ready threads run while a synchronous SPI transfer is progressing.
This is particularly important for DMA-backed full-screen display writes,
where busy polling otherwise serializes rendering and wire transfer on the
same CPU.

---
 drivers/spi/spi_esp32_spim.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi_esp32_spim.c b/drivers/spi/spi_esp32_spim.c
index 17de8aa..0ca6612 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi_esp32_spim.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi_esp32_spim.c
@@ -365,7 +365,9 @@ static int IRAM_ATTR spi_esp32_transfer(const struct device *dev)
 	spi_context_update_tx(&data->ctx, data->dfs, transfer_len_frames);
 
 	while (!spi_hal_usr_is_done(hal)) {
-		/* nop */
+		if (!k_is_pre_kernel()) {
+			k_sleep(K_MSEC(1));
+		}
 	}
 
 #if defined(SOC_GDMA_SUPPORTED)
-- 
2.51.0
